From 0a23123d5a6fea0c7ab0641884c38f14eca6a139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x87 transfers: bytes beside a store's form (#2924)

The mutation round's survivor y4 compared a record's form with the byte
after it: no fixture's store had a nonzero vvvv. The candidate fixture's
records now carry vvvv and decoration bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgbxngY8HBj6wFPMjAjgYD
Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>
---
 src/buster/compiler/tier1_x87_transfer_test.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/buster/compiler/tier1_x87_transfer_test.c b/src/buster/compiler/tier1_x87_transfer_test.c
index 5a62b439..52d27fb4 100644
--- a/src/buster/compiler/tier1_x87_transfer_test.c
+++ b/src/buster/compiler/tier1_x87_transfer_test.c
@@ -159,6 +159,9 @@ static void tier1_x87_transfer_candidate_bounds(Tier1WideTest* test)
             {
                 const uint32_t kind = (r * 7 + count) % 5;
                 records[r] = tier1_x87_transfer_memory(kind == 1 ? X86_FORM_FLD_M80 : X86_FORM_FSTP_M80, X86_REGISTER_RSP, (int32_t)(16 * r));
+                // The bytes beside the form are no part of it.
+                records[r].vvvv = (uint8_t)(r | 1);
+                records[r].decorations = (uint8_t)r;
                 tokens[r] = kind == 2 ? r + 1 : r;
                 eligible[r] = kind != 3;
                 mixed |= (uint64_t)(kind != 1 && kind != 2 && kind != 3) << r;
-- 
